# Coding Standards

## Scope and design

- **Minimize diff** — smallest change that fixes the root cause. No drive-by refactors.
- **No over-engineering** — no extra abstractions for one-off cases; inline when clearer.
- **Match existing style** — naming, imports, error handling, and file layout of the surrounding code.
- **Comments** — only for non-obvious business logic; code should read clearly without noise.

## TypeScript / agents

- Shared types live in `shared/src/`; agent-specific logic stays in `agents/<name>/src/`.
- Use `.js` extensions in ESM imports (`from './foo.js'`).
- Prefer existing helpers (`postWithRetry`, `log`, `agentFetch`) over duplicating HTTP logic.
- Env vars: `process.env['VAR_NAME']` with sensible defaults documented in helm/compose.

## Inter-agent HTTP (critical)

Agents enforce `SRE_AUTH_STRICT` + `SRE_INTERNAL_TOKEN` on non-`/health` routes.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — 401 from investigator/orchestrator
await fetch(`${INVESTIGATOR_URL}/get?...`);

// ✅ GOOD — commander
import { agentFetch } from './agent-fetch.js';
await agentFetch(`${INVESTIGATOR_URL}/get?...`);

// ✅ GOOD — other agents / shared
import { internalAuthHeaders } from '../../../shared/src/internal-auth.js';
await fetch(url, { headers: internalAuthHeaders({ 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }), ... });
```

Console BFF uses `internalAuthHeaders()` in `proxyJson()` — ensure console pod has `SRE_INTERNAL_TOKEN` after secret changes (rollout restart).

## Helm / Kind

- Wire `{{- include "sre-bot.internalAuthEnv" . | nindent 12 }}` on every deployment using `createInternalAuthMiddleware`.
- Set `secrets.sreInternalToken` in Kind deploy (`deploy-kind.sh` defaults to `sre-bot-local-dev-token`).
- After secret or env updates, restart pods that mount the secret — env is fixed at pod start.

## Security

- Never commit secrets (`.env.local`, API keys). Use `helm/sre-bot/secrets.example.yaml` as reference.
- Use timing-safe auth checks (`shared/src/internal-auth.ts`); do not roll custom token compare.
